@PC sound effect options
All numbers in this menu are floating point numbers that can have optional
fractional parts, and you may use "e" or "E" preceding an exponent part,
which is the base ten exponent. All of these numbers must be positive, and
cannot be zero or negative.

þ Whole note duration: The duration of a whole note in seconds. The default
value is 1.81 seconds.

þ Percussion rate: Determines how fast percussion notes are played; does
not affect the duration of the note. Higher numbers are faster. The default
value is 1.81, to match the default value of the whole note duration, but
the units are different for this value.

þ Base overtone frequency: The base frequency for notes in the overtone
scale in hertz. The default is 32 hertz.

þ Base undertone frequency: The base frequency for notes in the undertone
scale in hertz. The default is 2048 hertz.

You can also set the frequency for normal notes, in the scale of twelve
notes (from C to B). You cannot change the names of the notes, nor set
different frequencies for enharmonic notes. There are two ways of doing
this, either by setting the frequency of the lowest note and having the
rest handled automatically by 12-TET, or by setting the frequency of each
note of the scale individually in which case higher octaves are handled
automatically by doubling the frequency of the previous octave.

